<!--
  A payment status report answering a pain.001 this service sent, held to the
  official pain.002.001.10 schema in tests/schemas/.

  It is deliberately a partial acceptance, because that is the case a parser
  gets wrong: the group says PART, the payment block says ACCP, and one of the
  two transactions inside it is RJCT with a reason code. A reader that took "the
  status" from any one level would report this message as accepted or as
  rejected, and both answers are wrong.

  OrgnlMsgId is the MsgId this service generates at accept time and stores on
  payment_order. It is the join, and it is why the status report is worth
  downloading at all.
-->
